<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns two secondary credits.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns two secondary credits.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico has placed two of the three credits whereby it sought to inject 3.995 billion pesos in the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The credits were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>CREDIT AUCTIONS  TERM     MAX    MIN     AVERAGE  BIDS BIDDERS</p>
<p>1.000  bln pesos 3 days   31.33  31.00   31.18    5    3</p>
<p>1.000  bln pesos 2 days   31.30  31.50   30.18    8    4</p>
<p>1.995  bln pesos 1  day</p>
<p>NOTE - The maximum, minimum and average are percentages.</p>
<p>- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9500</p>
</text>
